    {
      "id": "library/hmans-2026-beans-readme/blocks/prose-s005-installation",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Installation",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s005-installation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "## Installation\n\nWe'll need to do three things:\n\n1. Install the `beans` CLI tool.\n2. Configure your project to use it.\n3. Configure your coding agent to interact with it.\n\nEither download Beans from the [Releases section](https://github.com/hmans/beans/releases), or install it via Homebrew:\n\n```bash\nbrew install hmans/beans/beans\n```\n\nAlternatively, install directly via Go:\n\n```bash\ngo install github.com/hmans/beans@latest\n```",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/hmans-2026-beans-readme/blocks/prose-s006-configure-your-project",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Configure Your Project",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s006-configure-your-project.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "## Configure Your Project\n\nInside the root directory of your project, run:\n\n```bash\nbeans init\n```\n\nThis will create a `.beans/` directory and a `.beans.yml` configuration file at the project root. All of it is meant to be tracked in your version control system.\n\nFrom this point onward, you can interact with your Beans through the `beans` CLI. To get a list of available commands:\n\n```bash\nbeans help\n```\n\nBut more importantly, you'll want to get your coding agent set up to use it. Let's dive in!",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
